This function creates a new `App::Sqitch::Plan::ChangeList` object, passing in the plan object and the `event` parameter (if present) from the `%p` hash. It then iterates over the plan lines, skipping any lines that are not `App::Sqitch::Plan::Change` objects. For each change, it checks if the change should be included in the change list using the `should_include` method of the `App::Sqitch::Plan::ChangeList` object. If it should be included, it adds the change to the change list using the `add` method. Finally, it returns the change list.

Note that the `should_include` method of the `App::Sqitch::Plan::ChangeList` object will determine which changes to include based on the `event` parameter passed to the `search_changes` function. If no `event` parameter was passed, all changes will be included. If an `event` parameter was passed, only changes with the specified event (e.g. `deploy` or `revert`) will be included.

